RECOVERED 2026-08-22====================`world' would not compile: every source begins #include "parame.inc", andparame.inc was not here.  It is not meant to be -- it is GENERATED.  Themakefile's `convert' target runs two small programs first:    vtxtcn   reads vtext.dat  ->  qtext.inc objdes.inc gtext.inc    vcnvrt   reads vocab.dat  ->  parame.inc vocab.inc verbtb.inc                                  locdat.inc objdat.inc trvtbl.incand only then builds the game.  `convert' itself is a `touch'ed timestampfile, not a program.The three data files the generators read -- vocab.dat, vtext.dat anddata.dat -- were missing from this tree.  They were still in the originalusenet archive, world.ar, which the import had read only partly; vtext.datwas in it as three pieces, vtext.dat.aa .ab and .ac, split on lineboundaries and joined back here.  They were extracted with the collection'sown ar2, which is the only thing that opens Carl Kreider's +AR0.0+ format.The .inc files are committed alongside them so that `tools/build.sh world'works with nothing else run first.  They are generated output and can bemade again at any time:    tools/build.sh vcnvrt vtxtcn      then run both in this directoryNothing in the game's own sources was changed.